# Config fragment merged onto radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig.
#
# Silences the "usb start" scan U-Boot otherwise runs on EVERY boot, whether
# or not anything is plugged into USB. Measured on hardware (bean gosd-uj4l,
# same session as dram-1gb.config's bench proof, bean gosd-6pfn): the
# "starting USB..." to "scanning usb for storage devices... 0 Storage
# Device(s) found" block costs ~4.5s of the board's 9.05s U-Boot phase,
# scanning four controllers to find nothing -- gosd images boot from mmc via
# extlinux and never from USB.
#
# WHERE the scan comes from, read at the pinned UBOOT_TAG (v2026.04):
# arch/arm/Kconfig's `config ARCH_SUNXI` hard-`select`s CONFIG_CMD_USB,
# CONFIG_USB_STORAGE and CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD whenever
# `DISTRO_DEFAULTS && USB_HOST` -- which is true here: DISTRO_DEFAULTS
# drives the distro_bootcmd/extlinux path this board's mmc boot depends on,
# and USB_HOST is select'd by the CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD/CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD
# host-controller drivers already in radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig. A Kconfig
# `select` cannot be turned off from a fragment -- `make olddefconfig`
# silently forces it back to y -- and disabling USB_HOST to break the
# condition would also remove real USB host/mass-storage support, not just
# the boot-time scan. So those three stay untouched here on purpose.
#
# The actual trigger is one level further down the SAME select chain, but
# it's a plain `default`, not a `select`: with CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD on,
# boot/Kconfig's `config PREBOOT` picks up `default "usb start" if
# USB_KEYBOARD`, and common/main.c's main_loop() runs whatever's in the
# "preboot" env var, unconditionally, before the boot-delay countdown even
# starts -- purely so a USB keyboard plugged in can interrupt autoboot on a
# desk. A `default` (unlike a `select`) IS overridable by an explicit
# fragment assignment, and this was confirmed against the real Kconfig
# engine: generating radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig's .config at the pinned tag
# with scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m + make olddefconfig shows
# CONFIG_PREBOOT="" sticks (CONFIG_PREBOOT_DEFINED drops out along with it,
# so main.c's `env_get("preboot")` returns NULL and the whole block is
# skipped) while CONFIG_CMD_USB, CONFIG_USB_STORAGE, CONFIG_USB_HOST,
# CONFIG_DM_USB and CONFIG_USB_GADGET (this board's MUSB peripheral mode,
# used by --usb-gadget) are all untouched. BOOTSTD, DISTRO_DEFAULTS and
# CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND ("run distro_bootcmd") are untouched too, so the mmc
# extlinux boot path this board actually uses is unaffected -- and if mmc
# ever failed, the "usb" boot_target later in distro_bootcmd's device list
# is still compiled in as a fallback; only the unconditional preboot probe
# is gone.
#
# NOT YET RE-MEASURED: authored without a container runtime or bench access,
# so this has been verified against the pinned tag's Kconfig sources and the
# real kconfig tooling (see above) but NOT through an actual U-Boot rebuild
# and hardware boot. The ~4.5s saving is a hypothesis from source reading,
# not a bench number -- re-measure before updating gosd-6pfn's baseline.
CONFIG_PREBOOT=""
